<DocsLayout title="NetworkX integration" kicker="12 / guide" description="Use a general-purpose graph library for graph manipulation and pass a reachq graph when you need these constructions.">
  <h2>Boundary</h2>
  <p>reachq is intentionally not a replacement for NetworkX or igraph. Convert at the boundary of your workflow, then keep the construction and validation steps explicit.</p>
  <p>The optional adapter lives in <code>reachq.io_networkx</code> and is not imported by the core package. Install the research/development dependencies that your adapter workflow needs and test the conversion on your own vertex types.</p>
</DocsLayout>
